; Copying everything used (objfpc): function[=](x) => e. Its copies are the
; variables and parameters of the routines around it that its body names
; (not globals, nor what it does not use); it must be a closure, and the
; copies are read-only.
; RUN: not %pcc --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/copyall/errors.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
; CHECK: errors.pas:13:8: error: a lambda that copies what it uses must be a closure: a 'reference to' type must be wanted here
; CHECK: errors.pas:14:24: error: cannot modify 'k', a copy made by this lambda (copies are read-only)
; CHECK-NOT: error:
;
; RUN: not %pcc --mode=objfpc -c %S/Inputs/copyall/syntax.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=SYNTAX %s
; SYNTAX: syntax.pas:8:17: error: expected name of a variable to copy
;
; The factory copies k and s, not g (a global), x (its parameter) or
; unused.
; RUN: %pcc --mode=objfpc --emit-ast %S/Inputs/copyall/ast.pas -o - | FileCheck --check-prefix=AST %s
; AST: FunctionDecl '$copy2' : TFn <11:11>
; AST-NEXT: ParamDecl 'k' : integer <11:33>
; AST-NEXT: ParamDecl 's' : string <11:48>
; AST-NEXT: FunctionDecl '$lambda1' : integer <11:11>
; AST: CallExpr '$copy2' : TFn <11:11>
; AST-NEXT: NameRefExpr 'k' parameter : integer <11:33>
; AST-NEXT: NameRefExpr 's' parameter : string <11:48>
; AST-NEXT: EmptyStmt <12:1>
